  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CARES: COVID-19 Assistance and Response for Enhanced Systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CARES assists the Philipine Government to respond to and recover from COVID-19 and strengthen its health and economic systems, in line with Australia&apos;s regional Vaccine Access and Health Security Initiative and the Philippines&apos; COVID-19 Country Response Plan. It includes short- to medium-term activities to achieve outcomes in health security and stability. These include: 1. provision of COVID-19 vaccine doses and delivery support, health systems strengthening, and continuity of health service delivery; 2. mental health and psychosocial support to vulnerable groups, enhancing child protection, and helping prevent gender-based violence, 3. scaling up risk informed and shock responsive social protection and supporting social cohesion in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao and, 4. improving collaboration among CSOs, local and national governments to make recovery efforts more effective.</narrative>
  </description>
